---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Y.Org"
  description="Learn about Y.Org, its vision, design principles and goals."
>
  <div class="breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Index</a>
    <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
    <span>About</span>
  </div>

  <header class="about-header">
    <h1>About Y.Org</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      Y.Org is a project exploring the evolution of the
      classic X.Org window system, with a focus on security,
      transparency and user control.
    </p>
  </header>

  <article class="about-content">
    <section>
      <h2>What is Y.Org?</h2>

      <p>
        Y.Org is an open-source project focused on the
        foundations of graphical environments for Linux and
        other Unix-like operating systems.
      </p>

      <p>
        The project aims to investigate a different approach
        to window system design, reconsidering how applications
        interact with the graphical environment and how those
        interactions can be managed securely.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>From X.Org to Y.Org</h2>

      <p>
        X.Org has played an important role in the history of
        graphical environments on Unix-like systems. Y.Org
        takes inspiration from this legacy while exploring
        alternative architectural ideas for the future.
      </p>

      <p>
        Y.Org is not intended to be presented as a finished
        replacement for X.Org. Compatibility, migration and
        integration with existing graphical software require
        further research and design.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Why Y.Org?</h2>

      <p>
        Graphical applications need access to shared resources
        to provide a useful desktop experience. However, that
        access should not automatically imply unrestricted
        control over the graphical session.
      </p>

      <p>
        Y.Org explores whether clearer permission boundaries
        and explicit user authorization can improve security
        without sacrificing usability.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Design principles</h2>

      <div class="principle">
        <h3>User control</h3>
        <p>
          Users should have meaningful control over sensitive
          operations performed within their graphical session.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="principle">
        <h3>Security by design</h3>
        <p>
          Security should be considered from the beginning of
          the architecture, rather than added as an afterthought.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="principle">
        <h3>Transparency</h3>
        <p>
          The system's behavior, permission model and technical
          decisions should be documented clearly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="principle">
        <h3>Open development</h3>
        <p>
          The project aims to make its source code, development
          process and design discussions accessible to the
          open-source community.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Technology</h2>

      <p>
        Y.Org will be developed primarily using Rust and Vulkan.
        Rust will serve as the main implementation language,
        while Vulkan will be used for graphics-related work.
      </p>

      <p>
        These technologies are intended to support a system
        designed with security, performance, reliability and
        user control in mind. The exact architecture and the
        responsibilities of each component will be defined
        throughout development.
      </p>

      <p>
        Y.Org is still in its early stages, and its technical
        design may evolve as the project progresses.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Philosophy</h2>

      <p>
        The philosophy of Y.Org is simple: the user should
        remain in control of the system, and that includes
        the applications running within it.
      </p>

      <p>
        A graphical environment should serve its user rather
        than give applications unrestricted authority over
        the session. Applications should have access to the
        resources they need to operate, but that access should
        respect the user's authority and the system's security
        boundaries.
      </p>

      <p>
        Y.Org aims to explore a model in which sensitive
        graphical operations can be governed by clear
        permissions and explicit user authorization. Users
        should be able to understand what an application is
        requesting and make informed decisions about granting
        access.
      </p>

      <p>
        Security should not mean taking control away from the
        user. Instead, it should help protect the user's
        freedom to decide how their own system behaves.
      </p>

      <p>
        Ultimately, Y.Org is guided by the principle that
        the computer belongs to its user. The system should
        enforce its security rules transparently while
        keeping the user, rather than individual applications,
        at the center of control.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Current status</h2>

      <p>
        Y.Org is in an early stage of development. Its
        architecture and design are still evolving, and the
        ideas described on this website should be understood
        as project goals rather than completed features.
      </p>

      <p>
        Follow the project's progress on the{" "}
        <a href="/development/">Development</a> page or explore
        its source code on{" "}
        <a
          href="https://github.com/The-Y-Org-Project/Y.Org"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-header {
    padding: 20px 0 25px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #c8ccd1;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }

  .about-header .lead {
    max-width: 790px;
    color: #54595d;
    font-family: "Gelasio", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .about-content {
    max-width: 850px;
  }

  .about-content section {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
  }

  .about-content h2 {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .about-content p {
    margin-bottom: 13px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .principle {
    padding: 12px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #eaecf0;
  }

  .principle:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .principle h3 {
    margin: 0 0 5px;
    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: bold;
  }

  .principle p {
    margin: 0;
    color: #54595d;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .about-header .lead {
      font-size: 17px;
    }
  }
</style>
